<section class="bhd-page__feature"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Creator principle</p><h2>Useful content beats forced promotion</h2><p>The strongest creator relationship starts with a real reason to talk about hydration. That might be endurance training, long shifts, travel, heat, active living, recovery routines or another setting where fluid and electrolyte decisions already matter to the audience.</p><p>Best Hydrate prefers credible, useful communication over scripted enthusiasm. A creator should be able to explain the relationship clearly and speak in a voice that still feels like their own.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Ways to work together</p><h2>Different content relationships need different terms</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3">
  <article><h3>Product Seeding & Trials</h3><p>Product may be provided for genuine evaluation or content consideration without requiring positive coverage. Any gifted relationship should still be disclosed where appropriate.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Educational & Editorial Content</h3><p>Creators can help translate hydration concepts into practical, audience-relevant stories when statements remain accurate and within scope.</p></article>
  <article><h3>Campaigns & Licensed Creative</h3><p>Paid campaigns, user-generated creative, usage rights or performance-based arrangements can be defined when the concept, deliverables and terms are agreed in advance.</p></article>
</div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__split"><div class="bhd-page__split-media"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/5077064/pexels-photo-5077064.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Creator planning digital content at a desk" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="bhd-page__split-copy"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">What we look for</p><h2>Relevance, trust and a clear point of view</h2><p>Follower count is only one signal. We also care about audience relevance, content quality, consistency, credibility and whether the creator's normal subject matter gives hydration a natural place to appear.</p><p>Micro-creators, specialists and community voices can be especially useful when they have a trusted relationship with a defined audience. The goal is not reach at any cost. It is useful communication to people for whom the message actually matters.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">What we do not ask for</p><h2>No hidden sponsorship or manufactured outcomes</h2><p>Best Hydrate does not ask creators to conceal compensation, fabricate a testimonial, claim a guaranteed result, or present an individual experience as proof of medical or athletic efficacy.</p><p>Where a post involves a paid, gifted, affiliate or other material relationship, disclosure should be clear enough that the audience can understand the connection.</p></article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout"><span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Content standard</span><h3>Be useful first. Be transparent always.</h3><p>Credibility compounds when the audience understands both the message and the relationship behind it.</p></aside>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Good starting information</p><h2>Make the first conversation easy to assess</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4"><article><h3>Audience</h3><p>Who follows you, where they are and what they come to you for.</p></article><article><h3>Channels</h3><p>The platforms and formats where you are strongest.</p></article><article><h3>Concept</h3><p>Why Best Hydrate fits and what useful content you have in mind.</p></article><article><h3>Terms</h3><p>Any timing, product, compensation, licensing or deliverable expectations.</p></article></div></section>

